```apex
/**
 * NPSP TDTM handler. It creates a "Major gift thank-you call" Task when an Opportunity
 * becomes Closed Won with Amount >= 5000.
 *
 * Register it with an npsp__Trigger_Handler__c record:
 *   Class = OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM, Object = Opportunity,
 *   Trigger Action = AfterInsert;AfterUpdate, Load Order = 5, Asynchronous = false.
 *
 * There is no Apex trigger. NPSP's TDTM dispatcher calls run(). Deactivating the
 * Trigger Handler record stops this logic from running.
 *
 * Governor usage: no SOQL. Closed Won is read from the standard IsWon field, which is
 * populated on trigger records. No DML of its own: the Tasks are returned in the
 * DmlWrapper, and NPSP inserts them in one bulk DML.
 */
global without sharing class OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM extends npsp.TDTM_Runnable {

    @TestVisible
    private static final Decimal MAJOR_GIFT_THRESHOLD = 5000;
    @TestVisible
    private static final String TASK_SUBJECT = 'Major gift thank-you call';

    global override npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper run(
        List<SObject> newlist,
        List<SObject> oldlist,
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action triggerAction,
        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objResult
    ) {
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper dmlWrapper = new npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper();

        Boolean isInsert = triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AfterInsert;
        Boolean isUpdate = triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AfterUpdate;
        if ((!isInsert && !isUpdate) || newlist == null || newlist.isEmpty()) {
            return dmlWrapper;
        }

        Map<Id, Opportunity> oldMap = new Map<Id, Opportunity>();
        if (isUpdate && oldlist != null) {
            for (SObject so : oldlist) {
                oldMap.put(so.Id, (Opportunity) so);
            }
        }

        List<Task> tasks = new List<Task>();
        for (SObject so : newlist) {
            Opportunity opp = (Opportunity) so;
            if (!qualifies(opp)) {
                continue;
            }
            if (isUpdate) {
                Opportunity oldOpp = oldMap.get(opp.Id);
                // Skip gifts that already qualified before this update.
                if (oldOpp != null && qualifies(oldOpp)) {
                    continue;
                }
            }
            tasks.add(new Task(
                Subject = TASK_SUBJECT,
                Priority = 'High',
                Status = 'Not Started',
                WhatId = opp.Id,
                WhoId = (Id) opp.get('npsp__Primary_Contact__c'),
                OwnerId = opp.OwnerId,
                ActivityDate = opp.CloseDate == null ? null : opp.CloseDate.addDays(3)
            ));
        }

        if (!tasks.isEmpty()) {
            dmlWrapper.objectsToInsert.addAll((List<SObject>) tasks);
        }
        return dmlWrapper;
    }

    private static Boolean qualifies(Opportunity opp) {
        return opp.IsWon == true
            && opp.Amount != null
            && opp.Amount >= MAJOR_GIFT_THRESHOLD;
    }
}
```

Change from the previous version: the handler no longer runs any SOQL query. It previously queried `OpportunityStage` to find which stages count as Closed Won. Together with whatever else runs in the same transaction, that pushed the total over the one-query limit. It now reads the standard `Opportunity.IsWon` field instead. That field is populated on both the new and old records in after triggers and still respects custom won stages.

The rest is unchanged:
- **No DML of its own.** Tasks are still returned in `DmlWrapper.objectsToInsert`, and NPSP inserts them in one bulk DML statement.
- **No duplicate tasks.** A task is skipped when the old record already met both conditions, so editing a gift that already qualified creates nothing.
- **Running only through TDTM.** There is still no Apex trigger, so the handler runs only while its Trigger Handler record is active.

